# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-clautolisp-backend-semantic-parity — keep direct and subprocess clautolisp semantics identical
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-alfe-clautolisp-backend-semantic-parity
#+DATE: 2026-10-06

* Context

=alfe --clautolisp= has two execution variants:

- the default =--backend direct= embeds the clautolisp runtime in alfe;
- =--backend subprocess= launches the standalone =clautolisp= program.

These are two transports for the same engine, not two user-visible products.
Selecting the subprocess variant for isolation must not change the meaning or
availability of an option shared by alfe and clautolisp.

The divergence was observed in SCHME job 527154 with alfe 2.2.150:

#+begin_example
alfe: alfe CLAUTOLISP backend error (phase BOOTSTRAP):
Failed to initialise the clautolisp runtime:
no reader codec registered for format :DWG [RUNTIME-INIT-FAILED]
#+end_example

The invocation already contained =--clautolisp --host cador --dwg
Schema_Test.dwg=.  The temporary downstream workaround is to add =--backend
subprocess= to the SCHME cador suites.

* Problem

The two variants do not contain the same runtime capabilities.

=clautolisp/clautolisp-tool= depends on =clautolisp/drawing-dwg=, so the
standalone program registers the =:DWG= reader/writer codec.  The alfe tool
depends on =autolisp-front-end=, whose in-process clautolisp graph does not
load that optional system.  Consequently the same =--dwg= option is parsed
and forwarded to =host-open-startup-drawing= in direct mode, but fails before
the action plan runs because no DWG codec is registered.

This is a semantic difference, not merely an implementation detail:

#+begin_example
alfe --clautolisp --host cador --dwg file.dwg ...
alfe --clautolisp --backend subprocess --host cador --dwg file.dwg ...
#+end_example

The first and second commands are expected to expose the same clautolisp
features and observable results.  A caller must not need to know which ASDF
systems happen to have been baked into the alfe image.

The risk is broader than =--dwg=.  Shared CLI parsing, duplicated direct-mode
initialisation and selective subprocess forwarding can let any present or
future option work in only one variant, or use different defaults, environment
variables, diagnostics, side effects or exit statuses.

* Proposal

1. Define one explicit capability and option contract for alfe's clautolisp
   backend.  Both variants must consume the same resolved configuration.
2. Make the direct alfe image load every clautolisp subsystem required to
   implement that contract.  In particular, load =clautolisp/drawing-dwg= so
   =--dwg= registers the same codec as the standalone program while preserving
   lazy loading of the native library.
3. Derive subprocess arguments and direct-mode initialisation from the same
   option descriptors or resolved configuration, instead of maintaining two
   independent lists.
4. Audit every option accepted for =--clautolisp=, including host, dialect,
   drawing, source/file/terminal encodings, init policy, action ordering,
   debugger/error policy, dribble, DCL/UI selection, optimisation and future
   shared options.  Remove documented direct/subprocess exceptions by
   implementing equivalent behaviour rather than silently ignoring an option.
5. When exact parity is structurally impossible, reject the option explicitly
   and identically before starting either engine.  Do not accept it and then
   silently change its meaning according to the backend variant.

* Acceptance criteria

- Both commands above open the same DWG and run the same action plan with the
  same observable AutoLISP state, stdout, stderr and exit status.
- =alfe --clautolisp --dwg FILE= works in the default direct variant whenever
  the installed native DWG libraries support the subprocess variant.
- A table-driven regression suite runs every option common to the clautolisp
  backend once with =--backend direct= and once with =--backend subprocess=.
- The parity suite compares resolved configuration, action ordering, output,
  diagnostics, exit status and relevant file/drawing side effects.
- Adding a new shared clautolisp option requires adding it once to the common
  option contract; CI fails if either variant does not consume it.
- =alfe --help=, the alfe user manual, man page and specifications state the
  semantic-parity guarantee and no longer document backend-variant differences
  for shared options.
- The SCHME workaround (=--backend subprocess= on the cador suites) can be
  removed after a release containing the fix is consumed.

